----- set vs frozenset

	set - defined as a = {1,23,3} and mutable
	frozenset - defined as a = frozenset(iterable) and immutable.
		  - we cannot pass values directly in frozenset, we need to pass iterable only.
	

----- break, continue, pass

	break -  The break statement terminates the loop immediately and the control flows to the statement after the body of the loop.
	continue - The continue terminates the current iteration of the statement, skips the rest of the code in the current iteration and the control flows to the next iteration of the loop.
	pass - the pass keyword in Python is generally used to fill up empty blocks and is similar to an empty statement
		

----- What are modules,library and packages in Python?

	module - Simple python file contains functions and variables 
	package - The package is a simple directory having collections of modules.
		ex. numpy, pandas
	library - The library is having a collection of related functionality of codes that allows you to perform many tasks without writing your code.
		ex. matplotlib, pygame
	

----- What are global, protected and private attributes in Python?

	global -    public variable defined in global scope. (Example - global config)
	protected - attribute define with the underscore _ prefix to their identifier, they are accessible only in class. They can still be accessed and modified from outside the class they are defined using inheritance.
	private -   attribute with double underscore __ prefix to their identifier, they cannot be accessed or modified from the outside directly and will result in an AttributeError if such an attempt is made

----- use of self and __init__ in python

	self -     used to represent instance of the class, it directly point to the object of the class. By this we can access attributes and methods of class
	__init__ - constructor which is automatically called when instance created


